  "question": {
    "text": "Ferrous sulphate heptahydrate is used to fortify foods with iron. The amount (in grams) of the salt required to achieve <math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> of iron in <math><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of wheat is ____________.<br />Atomic weight: <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>55.85</mn><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32.00</mn><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16.00</mn></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4.95",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Formula of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ppm</mi></math>&nbsp;is as follow-</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ppm</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>weight</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>solute</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>weight</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>solution</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math></p><p><math><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8201;</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>&#8201;</mo><mi>F</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Or mass fe <math><mo>=</mo><mi></mi><mn>1</mn><mi>g</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>O</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>278</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />56g in 1 mole<br /><math><mn>1</mn><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>56</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>56</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>278</mn><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.96</mn><mi>g</mi></math></p><p>PPM is a concentration term and its full form is &quot;parts per million&quot; and it also can be expressed as milligrams per liter (mg/L). This measurement is the mass of a chemical or contaminate per unit volume of water.&nbsp;</p>"
  }
